From aba19a9f6ce97dc8a889059dc11254dccca597f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stefan <kloterstefan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 12:30:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Vizz: fit the app slot (FM-1 built without the second
 core)

Skiff 1.4 left 212 bytes of the FM-1's app slot (XIP, 0x8DFBC) with
the JieLi toolchain 20260730.1; SEQ MIDI OUT alone needs more. What
saves without changing anything the unit does:

- the globals SEQ MIDI OUT and its mutes added (seq_clk_acc, the CC 103
  state) in .pool, zeroed at boot: among the merged globals they moved
  others past the short offsets and grew code all over (fm1_main,
  ui_input, the drawing, the editor: about 2 KB)
- ABOUT's VIZZ in V, which has the Z; L stays Skiff's set
- the credits' VIZZ line shorter, Skiff's own credit as it was
- tools/size_fns.py: minsize for the main-loop functions of
  midi_learn.c, master.c, throw.c, mod.c, perform.c, launch.c, fx.c
  and audio.c (what an interrupt reaches stays -Os; no engine file:
  their render functions are reached through ENGINES[], which
  isr_reach does not follow)

That leaves 712 bytes over. build.py therefore builds the FM-1 without
the second core (FELUCCA_CPU2=0, Skiff's own option): MENU > SYSTEM >
CPU 2 CORES (beta, 1 CORE by default) is gone; 2184 bytes stay free.
FELUCCA_CPU2=1 builds it in again (and does not fit).

run_tests.sh: SEQ MIDI OUT, the UI tests and the UI renders also as
the FM-1 build has it (FELUCCA_CPU2=0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
